-- title:
--   Psd Contraction Comm Sandwich Le
-- statement:
--   **A commuting positive contraction contracts a positive operator by sandwiching.**
--
--   Let $S$ and $B$ be operators on a finite Hilbert space. Assume that $S$ is positive semidefinite and satisfies $S\le I$, that $B$ is positive semidefinite, and that $S$ commutes with $B$.
--
--   Then the operator order obeys
--
--   $$
--   SBS\le B.
--   $$
--
--   This is the sandwich domination estimate used to bound the complete and incomplete recurrence-weight contributions in the self-consistency context calculation.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.psd_contraction_comm_sandwich_le`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
